# Claude #2e: SWAP THEOREM check in Tide. Each line: a deck with card 1 at the bottom, then the same deck with cards n-1 and n swapped.
# Prints n, then (length of deck with n-1 above n) minus (length with n above n-1); the theorem says 2^(n-3).
use stdlib
: n 1 dig ;
: card 10 + dig ;
: setcard 10 + bury ;
: tuck 1 card 5 bury 1 1 [ drop dup 1 + card over setcard 1 + dup 5 dig < ] drop drop 5 dig 5 dig setcard ;
: play 0 1 card 1 = 0 = [ drop tuck 1 + 1 card 1 = 0 = ] drop ;
5 1 bury 4 1 setcard 3 2 setcard 5 3 setcard 2 4 setcard 1 5 setcard play 7 bury 5 1 setcard 3 2 setcard 4 3 setcard 2 4 setcard 1 5 setcard play 7 dig swap - n . . cr
